ing."]}, "overview": "Central Florida's 9th District pairs a Democratic incumbent, Darren Soto, with a Republican-leaning electorate, making him one of the cycle's most vulnerable House Democrats. Most professional raters call the race a Republican flip, and prediction markets give Soto roughly a three-in-ten chance of holding on. The lone public poll, from August, showed the candidates tied.\n\nSoto retains real strengths: a large cash advantage, firefighter-union backing, Spanish-language outreach, and a record of constituent service including federal grants. Challenger Dan Green has raised substantial money and earned police-group endorsements. The race sits on the Republican side of tossup, but the polling record is thin enough that late developments could shift it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3442, "margin": -2.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2846, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2806, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3778, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3096, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3413, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2822, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.28, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2817, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2782, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2318, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3059, "margin": -3.0}]}